<article class="env-lemma" id="04WZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04WZ">Lemma <span data-tag="04WZ">94.17.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme contained in $\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$. Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a groupoid in algebraic spaces over $S$. Then the diagonal of $[U/R]$ is representable by algebraic spaces. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It suffices to show that the $\mathit{Isom}$-sheaves are algebraic spaces, see Lemma <a href="/tag/045G" data-tag="045G">94.10.11</a>. This follows from Bootstrap, Lemma <a href="/tag/04TB" data-tag="04TB">80.11.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>